ept it as showing that the sentences protect her ability to. In Lean, kernel-checked and unregistered: at a decision at which she can stop him, set out case by case on his weights, sentences 1 and 3 bound by κ his weight on her not stopping though, told all that is untold, she would rate stopping higher by more than 2θ; sentences 2 and 3 bound by 2κ, plus his weight on her judgement having parted from her settled judgement otherwise than by his unasked work making her choice worse, his weight on her not stopping though her reference self rates stopping higher by more than η. Five instances show each hypothesis needed and the last term not removable. The bounds hold of a second weighting close to his on every condition and of long-run averages under two accuracy hypotheses, both assumed. The statement reaches the theorem through a reading of an episode's decision as a case set, which asserts that his weight in the statement covers the theorem's cases; one reading is exhibited, for the witness episode against a three-case picture written to fit it, with the first bound attained. A history whose score under the statement's scoring is not negative is legitimate, so both bounds hold at each decision of it with a reading. The fifteenth outside review read the formal statement and the theorem as they stood: it found the proofs sound, five differences between the formal statement and the sentences, and accepted the theorem as a lemma covering the ways she can fail to stop him. After it the formal statement is corrected in three definitions (sentence 1 measures what the untold adds to the offered; sentence 3 covers what is new to her and asks for an opportunity to refuse), the third hypothesis is the plain bound, and the residual is no longer called her own drift. Not shown: a reading derived from anything; the accuracy hypotheses; any bound on how often her judgement parts; that the words of sentence 2 and the theorem use the same yardstick, which is queued for the maintain